## Description

This detection identifies **Windows Security Event ID 4672**, which is generated when special privileges are assigned to a newly authenticated user.

Event ID 4672 is commonly associated with administrative logons and accounts that possess elevated privileges such as **Administrator**, **SYSTEM**, **Local Service**, or other privileged accounts.

Monitoring privileged logons helps Security Operations Center (SOC) analysts identify administrative activity and detect unauthorized use of privileged credentials.

