# Analyst Notes

Event ID 4672 is one of the most valuable Windows Security events for monitoring privileged account usage. While it commonly appears during legitimate administrator logons, it should always be reviewed in context.

Unexpected privileged logons, especially when followed by PowerShell execution, service creation, scheduled tasks, or credential access activity, may indicate an attacker has obtained elevated privileges or compromised an administrative account.

This detection complements Detection 06 (Successful Logon) by highlighting sessions that have elevated permissions and require closer monitoring.
